  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Grammar Notes",
      "type": "block",
      "items": [
        {
          "heading": "Verbs",
          "lines": [
            "The word which tells us what a person, animal or thing does is known as a doing word or verb.",
            "Examples: eat, sing, play, bark, write"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "heading": "Am, Is, Are (present time, now)",
          "lines": [
            "Verbs also tell us what a person, animal or thing is.",
            "Is: with he, she, it or one name",
            "Am: with I",
            "Are: with you, we, they or many names"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "heading": "Was, Were (past time: yesterday or before)",
          "lines": [
            "Verbs also tell us what persons, animals and things were some time ago.",
            "Was: with I, he, she, it or one name",
            "Were: with you, we, they or many names"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "heading": "Has, Have, Had",
          "lines": [
            "'Has', 'have', 'had' are verbs. They show what a person, animal or thing possesses.",
            "Has: used with he, she, it or one name",
            "Have: used with I, you, we, they or many names",
            "Had: used for past time with all subjects"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
